These articles lists the world's deepest [[lake]]s.

==Lakes ranked by maximum depth==

This list contains all lakes whose maximum depth is reliably known to exceed {{Convert|400|m|ft|-2}}.

Geologically, the [[Caspian Sea]], like the [[Black Sea|Black]] and [[Mediterranean Sea|Mediterranean]] seas, is a remnant of the ancient [[Tethys Ocean]]. The deepest area is oceanic rather than continental crust. However, it is generally regarded by geographers as a large [[endorheic]] [[salt lake]]. 

Of the listed lakes; 10 have a deepest point above mean sea level. These are: [[Issyk-Kul]], [[Crater Lake]], [[Quesnel Lake|Quesnel]], [[Sarez Lake|Sarez]], [[Lake Toba|Toba]], [[Lake Tahoe|Tahoe]], [[Lake Kivu|Kivu]], [[Nahuel Huapi Lake|Nahuel Huapi]], [[Lake Van|Van]] and [[Lake Poso|Poso]]. The other lakes on the list reaches below sea level at their deepest points. This is a list, that includes the deepest lakes in the world (1 factor: depth). Not a list of the deepest [[cryptodepression]]s (2 factors: elevation compared with depth).

